    <string name="icon_editor_info">Adaptive and regular icons have significant differences. Regular icons are usually designed as a fixed image in PNG format and require multiple files with different dimensions to display properly in various sizes, offering less flexibility. In contrast, adaptive icons use two layers (background and foreground) in PNG and XML formats, allowing the icon to automatically adjust to different sizes and shapes, providing better optimization for devices and launchers. Adaptive icons were introduced as the standard starting from Android 8.0 (API Level 26) and offer better performance.</string>
